#: includes/class-amswap-abilities.php:64
msgid "Get admin menu"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-amswap-abilities.php:65
msgid ""
"Returns the top-level WordPress admin menu of one profile (default: "
"\"default\") in display order: each item's slug, title, whether it is hidden"
" and its preset group. Also returns where the profile's settings come from "
"(source: saved, preset, default, or inherit for a role that uses the default"
" menu), its effective settings (order, hidden, removed separators, separator"
" color, follows_default_order), the preset groups with the slugs no preset "
"pattern names, every profile with the number of users it applies to (count; "
"capped is true when count is a lower bound because the site has more users "
"than were counted), the agency domains and the number of agency accounts "
"(account_count; they always get the default profile) and the age of the menu"
" snapshot. User logins (users per profile, at most 50, and the agency "
"accounts) are left out unless include_users is true. Use it before "
"amswap/update-menu-order to get the exact slugs."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-amswap-abilities.php:74
msgid ""
"Also return the user logins of each profile and of the agency accounts. "
"These are personal data that the menu does not need, so leave this out "
"unless asked who a profile applies to."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-amswap-abilities.php:134
msgid "Update admin menu order"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-amswap-abilities.php:135
msgid ""
"Saves the top-level WordPress admin menu of one profile, as the settings "
"page does. It overwrites the order the profile had saved, and its hidden "
"items when hidden is given; separators of core and plugins that are left out"
" of order are removed. There is no undo other than sending the previous "
"order and hidden items again, so get them first with amswap/get-menu (or use"
" amswap/reset-menu-order if its source was not saved). profile is "
"\"default\" (agency accounts and roles without a profile) or a role. order "
"lists every slug in the wanted order; put \"separator-amswap\" entries where"
" a separator belongs (they are renumbered). For a role profile, leave order "
"out (or set follow_default_order) to follow the default order and only set "
"hidden. hidden replaces the hidden items; leave it out to keep the current "
"ones. separator_color (#rrggbb, \"\" for the default) is shared and only "
"accepted for the default profile. Slugs must exist in the menu (see "
"amswap/get-menu); unknown slugs are refused, except those already in the "
"profile's order or hidden items (such as the menu of a deactivated plugin), "
"which are kept. Afterwards the preset no longer applies to that profile "
"until amswap/reset-menu-order."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-amswap-abilities.php:142
msgid ""
"Every top-level slug in the wanted order, with \"separator-amswap\" entries "
"for separators. Required for the default profile."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-amswap-abilities.php:146
msgid "Role profiles only: follow the default order and ignore order."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-amswap-abilities.php:149
msgid ""
"Slugs to hide from the menu. Leave out to keep the current hidden items."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-amswap-abilities.php:153
msgid ""
"Default profile only: separator color as #rrggbb, or \"\" for the admin "
"color scheme default. Leave out to keep the current color."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-amswap-abilities.php:186
msgid "Reset admin menu order"
